WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:05.720
March has come and gone, and Netflix is springing
into the season with almost 40 Netflix originals

00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:06.730
for April.

00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:11.072
This month, you can leave the world behind
with the Lost in Space reboot, take an emotional

00:00:11.072 --> 00:00:15.500
ride through the midnight streets of L.A.
with 6 Balloons, and journey into the ancient

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:17.820
past with Troy: Fall of a City.

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:22.830
We'll also see new episodes of ongoing talk
shows like The Joel McHale Show and My Next

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:25.429
Guest Needs No Introduction with David Letterman.

00:00:25.429 --> 00:00:29.109
There's going to be something for even the
pickiest viewer on Netflix this April, so

00:00:29.109 --> 00:00:32.910
let's take a look at everything hitting the
streaming service, starting with the Netflix

00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:34.450
originals.

00:00:34.450 --> 00:00:35.450
Amateur

00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:40.730
In Amateur, 14-year-old Terron Forte is a
natural at basketball, but skill alone won't

00:00:40.730 --> 00:00:43.780
be enough when he's transferred to a prestigious
new school.

00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:47.400
With the odds stacked against him, Terron
will have to push harder than ever to live

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:49.970
his dream of being a basketball star.

00:00:49.970 --> 00:00:51.810
In life, there are no free throws.

00:00:51.810 --> 00:00:56.220
Shoot for the hoop when Amateur arrives on
April 6th.

00:00:56.220 --> 00:00:58.100
Fastest Car: Season 1

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:07.149
Like it says on the box, this upcoming series
is all about finding the fastest car.

00:01:07.149 --> 00:01:11.859
In each episode, a high-ticket supercar will
race a handful of souped up junkers to see

00:01:11.859 --> 00:01:16.460
whether money or hometown know-how is better
at reaching the checkered flag.

00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:21.380
Described as "sleeper cars" in Netflix's series
description, these secret speedsters could

00:01:21.380 --> 00:01:28.119
be anything from an '84 Honda to a minivan,
but they've all been turbocharged, gas-injected,

00:01:28.119 --> 00:01:32.420
and other car phrases to match the likes of
Porsches and Ferraris on the tarmac.

00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:35.740
Season 1 races onto Netflix on April 6th.

00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:37.539
Money Heist: Part 2

00:01:37.539 --> 00:01:41.619
If you haven't yet tuned in to Money Heist,
you don't know what you're missing.

00:01:41.619 --> 00:01:46.079
Despite its silly, satirical-sounding name,
Money Heist is a legitimately riveting crime

00:01:46.079 --> 00:01:51.359
drama about nine thieves attempting to pull
off the world's largest heist: break into

00:01:51.359 --> 00:01:56.079
the Spanish Royal Mint and print off more
than 2 billion euros.

00:01:56.079 --> 00:02:01.170
While the entire series aired in Spain in
2017, Netflix split the season into two parts

00:02:01.170 --> 00:02:04.030
for its US audience, just because they can.

00:02:04.030 --> 00:02:08.080
You can catch the second part of Money Heist
on April 6th.

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:09.470
Orbiter 9

00:02:09.470 --> 00:02:14.360
This Spanish sci-fi drama opens on a young
girl in an interstellar space pod on her way

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:15.870
to a distant planet.

00:02:15.870 --> 00:02:19.781
When her pod docks at a space station for
maintenance work, she falls in love with the

00:02:19.781 --> 00:02:24.380
tech guy — one of the first humans she's
ever met — and quickly finds out that she

00:02:24.380 --> 00:02:27.420
doesn't know the whole truth about her perilous
journey.

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:31.310
Take the ride when Orbiter 9 launches on April
6th.

00:02:31.310 --> 00:02:32.860
The 4th Company

00:02:32.860 --> 00:02:38.060
This film swept Mexico's Ariel Awards and
was reportedly on the shortlist for Best Foreign

00:02:38.060 --> 00:02:42.440
Language Film at the 89th Academy Awards before
it was dropped from the list.

00:02:42.440 --> 00:02:47.150
The 4th Company is based on the true story
of a prison football team that moonlighted

00:02:47.150 --> 00:02:52.140
as a violent enforcement gang in one of Mexico's
most notorious penitentiaries.

00:02:52.140 --> 00:02:56.840
To preserve the sense of realism, the filmmakers
decided to take the production inside the

00:02:56.840 --> 00:03:00.370
actual prison and use real inmates as extras.

00:03:00.370 --> 00:03:05.140
It doesn't get any closer to home than that,
and you can experience the whole wild story

00:03:05.140 --> 00:03:06.560
on April 6th.

00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:08.820
6 Balloons

00:03:08.820 --> 00:03:13.510
Starring Dave Franco and Abbi Jacobson, 6
Balloons details a harrowing night in Los

00:03:13.510 --> 00:03:19.370
Angeles as a woman desperately tries to find
a detox center for her heroin-addicted brother.

00:03:19.370 --> 00:03:23.480
Complicating their search is the man's two-year-old
daughter, who's along for the ride.

00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:27.760
Early reviews of this South by Southwest entry
have praised the film's riveting portrayal

00:03:27.760 --> 00:03:32.960
of addiction — including the emotional addiction
of a sister who can't bring herself to break

00:03:32.960 --> 00:03:35.650
away from the brother destroying her life.

00:03:35.650 --> 00:03:37.780
Take the ride on April 6.

00:03:37.780 --> 00:03:39.570
Ram Dass, Going Home

00:03:39.570 --> 00:03:46.370
Ram Dass was one of the 1970s' most outspoken
counterculture gurus, an acid philosopher

00:03:46.370 --> 00:03:50.820
who toured the country giving lectures on
the nature of consciousness and life.

00:03:50.820 --> 00:03:57.571
Now, a little morbidly, Netflix is documenting
Ram Dass's final days with Ram Dass, Going

00:03:57.571 --> 00:04:03.580
Home, a conversation with the 86-year-old
guru as he awaits the end at his home in Hawaii.

00:04:03.580 --> 00:04:07.900
Ram Dass, Going Home will be released on April
6th.

00:04:07.900 --> 00:04:10.300
Troy: Fall of a City

00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:14.710
It's literally the oldest story in Western
literature, and we still can't get enough

00:04:14.710 --> 00:04:15.920
of the tale of Troy.

00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:20.600
This Netflix miniseries focuses on the love
affair between Paris and Helen of Troy and

00:04:20.600 --> 00:04:25.070
the advent of the Trojan War — you know,
everything that happened in the Brad Pitt

00:04:25.070 --> 00:04:29.440
movie, but with probably a lot more drama
and a lot less neck stabbing.

00:04:29.440 --> 00:04:34.170
Troy: Fall of a City has already premiered
on BBC One to mixed reviews.

00:04:34.170 --> 00:04:38.200
There's still plenty of time for the series
to pick up steam, but...we mean, you already

00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:39.850
know how it's going to end.

00:04:39.850 --> 00:04:42.490
People knew how it was going to end 800 years
ago.

00:04:42.490 --> 00:04:45.100
Anyway, check it out on April 6th.

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:47.060
Amo: Season 1

00:04:47.060 --> 00:04:52.410
Marking Netflix's first Filipino series, Amo
is a 12-part miniseries about the Philippine

00:04:52.410 --> 00:04:54.610
government's war on drug trafficking.

00:04:54.610 --> 00:04:59.860
The limited series was created by Brillante
Mendoza, who previously took home the award

00:04:59.860 --> 00:05:05.210
for best director at the 2009 Cannes [CAN]
Film Festival for his film Kinatay.

00:05:05.210 --> 00:05:10.270
Amo looks like another thrilling entry in
Mendoza's filmography of gritty, hard-hitting

00:05:10.270 --> 00:05:11.270
dramas.

00:05:11.270 --> 00:05:12.950
Look for it on April 9th.

00:05:12.950 --> 00:05:15.270
Lost in Space: Season 1

00:05:15.270 --> 00:05:20.800
The Lost in Space of the '60s is undoubtedly
a classic, but man, is it cheesy.

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:25.820
Full of cardboard sets and robots made from
the same plastic as hula hoops, it was still

00:05:25.820 --> 00:05:30.640
groundbreaking for its time, and the Robinson
family were everybody's favorite Saturday

00:05:30.640 --> 00:05:31.640
night heroes.

00:05:31.640 --> 00:05:34.020
"There is no longer a Will Robinson.

00:05:34.020 --> 00:05:37.800
I am now a useful cog in the vast all-powerful
mechanism."

00:05:37.800 --> 00:05:39.350
"Don't talk like that, Will.

00:05:39.350 --> 00:05:40.350
We'll help you."

00:05:40.350 --> 00:05:44.840
Is the Netflix remake going to carry on the
torch and delve into all the insane sci-fi

00:05:44.840 --> 00:05:49.580
shenanigans and moral conundrums that elevated
the original past its shoddy, budget-deprived

00:05:49.580 --> 00:05:50.790
special effects?

00:05:50.790 --> 00:05:52.170
Who knows!

00:05:52.170 --> 00:05:55.120
It has cool robots and a young, hip cast,
so there's that.

00:05:55.620 --> 00:05:58.080
"Danger Will Robinson."

00:05:58.080 --> 00:06:03.000
At this point, all we can do is wait until
April 13th to find out.

00:06:03.010 --> 00:06:05.260
Chef's Table: Pastry — Season 1

00:06:05.260 --> 00:06:10.960
A spinoff of the series Chef's Table, this
show focuses on pastry chefs and their culinary

00:06:10.960 --> 00:06:11.960
delights.

00:06:11.960 --> 00:06:13.910
A restaurant that only serves dessert?

00:06:13.910 --> 00:06:14.910
Why not?

00:06:14.910 --> 00:06:16.580
Exotic ice cream bars?

00:06:16.580 --> 00:06:17.580
You bet!

00:06:17.580 --> 00:06:18.850
Deep fried candy?

00:06:18.850 --> 00:06:19.850
Marry me.

00:06:19.850 --> 00:06:24.570
If your mouth is already watering, make a
reservation for Season 1 of Chef's Table:

00:06:24.570 --> 00:06:26.630
Pastry on April 13th.

00:06:26.630 --> 00:06:28.620
Come Sunday

00:06:28.620 --> 00:06:33.870
Starring Chiwetel Ejiofor and Jason Segel,
Come Sunday tells the surprising true story

00:06:33.870 --> 00:06:39.590
of Carlton Pearson, a bishop who was literally
dubbed a heretic after he started preaching

00:06:39.590 --> 00:06:42.620
that there was no such thing as a fiery afterlife.

00:06:42.620 --> 00:06:43.960
Should be a fun ride.

00:06:43.960 --> 00:06:46.020
Look for it on April 13th.

00:06:46.020 --> 00:06:48.120
Charité: Season 1

00:06:48.120 --> 00:06:52.210
This award-winning German historical drama
centers on a hospital in Berlin in the late

00:06:52.210 --> 00:06:53.400
1800s.

00:06:53.400 --> 00:06:58.150
The series focuses on the doctors of Charite
hospital as they try to deal with seemingly

00:06:58.150 --> 00:07:02.080
incurable diseases in a rapidly changing political
climate.

00:07:02.080 --> 00:07:05.050
Tune in for Season 1 on April 19th.

00:07:05.050 --> 00:07:06.830
Mercury 13

00:07:06.830 --> 00:07:11.550
Back in the heyday of space exploration, NASA
put a lot of emphasis on finding the right

00:07:11.550 --> 00:07:14.199
astronauts to be the first humans in space.

00:07:14.199 --> 00:07:19.430
Seven men were chosen to fly for the Mercury
program in the early '60s, but NASA also trained

00:07:19.430 --> 00:07:22.010
13 women for the same program.

00:07:22.010 --> 00:07:27.110
Even though they performed just as well in
training, this group, dubbed the Mercury 13,

00:07:27.110 --> 00:07:29.380
never flew on a single space mission.

00:07:29.380 --> 00:07:34.900
Netflix's Mercury 13 documentary looks at
these forgotten women and explores the reasons

00:07:34.900 --> 00:07:38.389
they didn't get the privilege of being among
the first people in space.

00:07:38.389 --> 00:07:42.080
Climb aboard when the documentary premieres
on April 20th.

00:07:42.080 --> 00:07:44.070
Dope: Season 2

00:07:44.070 --> 00:07:49.530
Netflix's drug war documentary series Dope
landed in December 2017 and immediately pulled

00:07:49.530 --> 00:07:51.290
in a strong viewership.

00:07:51.290 --> 00:07:56.650
The series looks at the drug issues from the
perspectives of buyers, sellers, and law enforcement.

00:07:56.650 --> 00:07:59.990
Whether you're a fan of the series or just
now hearing about it, you can look forward

00:07:59.990 --> 00:08:05.530
to more of the same stories when Season 2
of Dope hits the market on April 20th, appropriately

00:08:05.530 --> 00:08:06.730
enough.

00:08:06.730 --> 00:08:08.490
Dude

00:08:08.490 --> 00:08:13.520
Based on writer/director Olivia Milch's own
high school experiences, Dude follows four

00:08:13.520 --> 00:08:15.990
girls in their last few weeks of school.

00:08:15.990 --> 00:08:21.690
Kathryn Prescott, Lucy Hale, Alexandra Shipp,
and Awkwafina star, and the film arrives on

00:08:21.690 --> 00:08:24.040
Netflix on April 20th.

00:08:24.040 --> 00:08:25.720
Kodachrome

00:08:25.720 --> 00:08:30.860
In Netflix's upcoming Kodachrome, Ed Harris
and Jason Sudeikis star as a father and son

00:08:30.860 --> 00:08:34.940
who set off on a road trip to find the last
Kodachrome processing lab.

00:08:34.940 --> 00:08:38.839
It ought to be a real nostalgia-fueled trip
into memory lane for all those old-school

00:08:38.839 --> 00:08:40.620
photography buffs out there.

00:08:40.620 --> 00:08:42.550
Look for it on April 20th.

00:08:42.550 --> 00:08:44.810
The Letdown: Season 1

00:08:44.810 --> 00:08:49.420
Although it already aired in Australia in
2017, The Letdown will be making its way to

00:08:49.420 --> 00:08:51.270
American audiences this April.

00:08:51.270 --> 00:08:56.500
This comedy series focuses on Audrey, a young
mom trying to balance her life and relationships

00:08:56.500 --> 00:08:58.110
without going crazy.

00:08:58.110 --> 00:09:00.800
Season 1 lands on April 21st.

00:09:00.800 --> 00:09:02.570
Psychokinesis

00:09:02.570 --> 00:09:08.220
From Yeon Sang-ho, director of Train to Busan,
Psychokinesis is a Korean supernatural action

00:09:08.220 --> 00:09:12.830
thriller about a man who suddenly discovers
that he has telekinetic powers.

00:09:12.830 --> 00:09:16.910
But after using his newfound abilities to
help his daughter, he finds himself in the

00:09:16.910 --> 00:09:19.210
crosshairs of an unexpected threat.

00:09:19.210 --> 00:09:23.560
Whether you're a fan of Asian thrillers or
just love a good action movie, Psychokinesis

00:09:23.560 --> 00:09:25.310
looks like a film to check out.

00:09:25.310 --> 00:09:27.529
Look for it on April 25th.

00:09:27.529 --> 00:09:29.310
The Week Of

00:09:29.310 --> 00:09:33.980
The latest product of Adam Sandler's ongoing
deal with Netflix is The Week Of, a comedy

00:09:33.980 --> 00:09:38.050
about two parents during the week leading
up to their kids getting married.

00:09:38.050 --> 00:09:40.120
Sandler stars, along with Chris Rock.

00:09:40.120 --> 00:09:43.180
"I'm just saying, AC would be great."

00:09:43.180 --> 00:09:46.680
"You say it and we'll turn it on."

00:09:46.680 --> 00:09:48.000
"I said it."

00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:52.700
Get ready for all the awkward conversations
and ridiculous situations your brain can stand

00:09:52.700 --> 00:09:55.930
when The Week Of arrives on April 27th.

00:09:55.930 --> 00:09:57.670
The Rachel Divide

00:09:57.670 --> 00:10:02.480
You may remember Rachel Dolezal from her many
news appearances in 2015.

00:10:02.480 --> 00:10:08.410
As president of the Spokane branch of the
NAACP, Dolezal claimed to be African-American,

00:10:08.410 --> 00:10:10.270
but it turned out she was actually white.

00:10:10.270 --> 00:10:14.760
Dolezal subsequently resigned from her position
and faced a media backlash.

00:10:14.760 --> 00:10:19.270
Now, she's entering the spotlight again as
the subject of the Netflix documentary The

00:10:19.270 --> 00:10:20.690
Rachel Divide.

00:10:20.690 --> 00:10:24.250
Tune in for all the riveting plot twists on
April 27th.

00:10:24.250 --> 00:10:26.180
Bobby Kennedy for President

00:10:26.180 --> 00:10:31.080
If you've ever been curious about 1960s politics,
Netflix has you covered this April.

00:10:31.080 --> 00:10:37.710
"It's a statistical fact that Netflix releases
54 lengthy, high-brow documentaries everyday.

00:10:37.710 --> 00:10:41.480
And some people find it hard to keep up, like
this idiot."

00:10:41.480 --> 00:10:45.930
Bobby Kennedy for President will look into
Senator Robert Kennedy's 1968 presidential

00:10:45.930 --> 00:10:50.660
campaign and its tragic end when he was assassinated
in a hotel kitchen.

00:10:50.660 --> 00:10:53.140
Queue it up on April 27th.

00:10:53.140 --> 00:10:55.290
3%: Season 2

00:10:55.290 --> 00:11:00.730
As one of the most highly acclaimed Brazilian
shows in Netflix history, 3% is definitely

00:11:00.730 --> 00:11:02.570
one of those shows you need to watch.

00:11:02.570 --> 00:11:07.120
And with the second season due out soon, there's
never been a better time to get started.

00:11:07.120 --> 00:11:12.090
The first season set the stage for a futuristic
world where our planet is devastated by poverty

00:11:12.090 --> 00:11:17.140
and hunger, but a lucky 3% of the population
gets the chance to live a better life free

00:11:17.140 --> 00:11:19.300
from the struggles of the masses.

00:11:19.300 --> 00:11:22.290
Where Season 2 will take us is anyone's guess.

00:11:22.290 --> 00:11:24.320
Find out on April 27th.

00:11:24.320 --> 00:11:26.910
The New Legends of Monkey: Season 1

00:11:26.910 --> 00:11:30.840
Back in the '70s, there was a weird little
Japanese show called Monkey.

00:11:30.840 --> 00:11:35.730
It was about a magical monkey warrior who
traveled the land battling monsters and demons,

00:11:35.730 --> 00:11:37.580
and it had the best theme song ever.

00:11:38.080 --> 00:11:46.100
[singing] "Monkey Magic!"

00:11:46.600 --> 00:11:52.390
The New Legends of Monkey is a remake of that
old show, and follows basically the same premise:

00:11:52.390 --> 00:11:57.350
Monkey leads his band of misfit warriors across
ancient China, learning valuable lessons while

00:11:57.350 --> 00:11:58.960
they kung fu demons.

00:11:58.960 --> 00:12:00.519
Should be a good ol' time.

00:12:00.519 --> 00:12:03.230
Check it out on April 27th.

00:12:03.230 --> 00:12:04.700
Original stand-up comedy

00:12:04.700 --> 00:12:09.279
April will see a solid collection of new stand-up
comedy routines hitting the streaming service.

00:12:09.279 --> 00:12:14.080
French comedian Fary is showing up with his
new special Fary is the New Black on April

00:12:14.080 --> 00:12:20.071
3rd, followed by Greg Davies: You Magnificent
Beast on April 10th and Kevin James: Never

00:12:20.071 --> 00:12:22.490
Don't Give Up on April 24th.

00:12:22.490 --> 00:12:24.580
That does it for the Netflix originals.

00:12:24.580 --> 00:12:28.760
Now here are all the other films and TV shows
arriving on the streaming service in April

00:12:28.760 --> 00:12:30.390
2018.

00:12:30.390 --> 00:12:31.820
New movies

00:12:31.820 --> 00:12:37.160
April is bringing the big guns on the action
front - along with plenty of robots, sharks,

00:12:37.160 --> 00:12:38.430
and magical karate.

00:12:38.430 --> 00:12:41.370
"Those were $500 sunglasses, a------."

00:12:41.370 --> 00:12:46.820
Mortal Kombat, Deep Blue Sea, and Terminator
3: Rise of the Machines show up on the 1st,

00:12:46.820 --> 00:12:50.480
as well as Bad Boys and Pirates of the Caribbean:
Dead Man's Chest.

00:12:50.480 --> 00:12:55.649
You can also expect a whole lot of emotional,
character-driven dramas, such as Cold Mountain,

00:12:55.649 --> 00:13:00.700
Friday Night Lights, Life is Beautiful, and
Scarface, all of which arrive on the 1st.

00:13:00.700 --> 00:13:03.200
"Say hello to my little friend!"

00:13:04.690 --> 00:13:09.040
Later releases in the month aren't toning
down the drama, with the Will Smith-led Seven

00:13:09.040 --> 00:13:14.529
Pounds on the 15th, Chasing the Dragon on
the 19th, and The Man Who Knew Infinity on

00:13:14.529 --> 00:13:15.529
the 27th.

00:13:15.529 --> 00:13:19.450
On the flip side, only four new comedy films
are being added in April.

00:13:19.450 --> 00:13:24.660
Along Came Polly and Jackass 2.5 are coming
on the first, along with The Lost Boys.

00:13:24.660 --> 00:13:26.580
That's a comedy, right?

00:13:30.480 --> 00:13:31.480
"You're mine!"

00:13:32.180 --> 00:13:35.420
Similarly, the new documentary selection in
April will be slim pickings.

00:13:35.430 --> 00:13:40.610
On the first, Netflix is adding Big Time,
an exposé on the Danish architect Bjarke

00:13:40.610 --> 00:13:45.550
Ingels, and Fishpeople, a sweeping look at
people who spend most of their lives in the

00:13:45.550 --> 00:13:46.550
ocean.

00:13:46.550 --> 00:13:51.721
On the 5th, you can check out Behind the Curtain:
Todrick Hall, followed by the 2017 documentary

00:13:51.721 --> 00:13:54.769
Bill Nye: Science Guy on the 25th.

00:13:54.769 --> 00:14:00.300
For family fare, we'll be getting Cats &amp; Dogs,
Looney Tunes: Back in Action, and both Flintstones

00:14:00.300 --> 00:14:04.680
films, and those aren't even the highlights
for family movies on April 1st.

00:14:04.680 --> 00:14:10.280
That honor goes to The Iron Giant, the single
most emotionally scarring animated movie of

00:14:10.280 --> 00:14:11.290
all time.

00:14:11.290 --> 00:14:16.209
Also, the kids are bound to love the addition
of Despicable Me 3 on April 5th.

00:14:16.209 --> 00:14:20.490
But the family fun has to end sometime, so
after you're done crying your eyes out at

00:14:20.490 --> 00:14:26.310
The Iron Giant, lighten the mood with Seven
or the original Cabin Fever.

00:14:26.310 --> 00:14:32.170
Both of those arrive on the first, alongside
the 2009 Cabin Fever sequel and the vampire

00:14:32.170 --> 00:14:35.300
